  "title": "Berlin Biotope Area Factor – Implementation of guidelines helping to control temperature and runoff",
  "summary": "Inner city Berlin mandates green space in new building developments through the Biotope Area Factor (BAF). This regulation, part of the Berlin Landscape Programme since 1994, responds to urban climate challenges, reducing vulnerability by introducing green spaces to mitigate heatwaves and improve runoff management. In inner city Berlin, plans for the development of new buildings are subjected to the Berlin Landscape Programme, which includes a regulation requiring a proportion of the area to be left as green space: the Biotope Area Factor (BAF) or BFF (Biotop Flächenfaktor). All potential green areas, such as courtyards, roofs and walls are included in the BAF.",
